WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.153
Storm's coming. And you boys?

00:00:02.154 --> 00:00:05.122
Your daddy? You are
smack in the middle of it.

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:13.403
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:13.404 --> 00:00:14.916
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:16.819 --> 00:00:18.771
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:18.772 --> 00:00:21.034
Saving people, hunting things...

00:00:21.035 --> 00:00:22.759
The family business.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.534
Our whole lives have been
searching for this demon.

00:00:31.612 --> 00:00:33.430
Samuel Colt made a gun.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.628
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.512
We finally know who
this demon's gonna be,

00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:40.494
And now, we know how to kill it.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.939
More and more demons
are walking among us.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:52.193
You're not my dad. Dean,
what the hell's going on?

00:00:52.208 --> 00:00:53.679
I think he's possessed.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.859
My plans for you, Sammy...

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:00.274
You, and all the children like you.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.688
It's inside me. I can feel it. Shoot me!

00:01:08.692 --> 00:01:10.532
I can't hold on to it much longer!

00:01:14.986 --> 00:01:16.940
Why didn't you kill it?
We still got the colt.

00:01:16.944 --> 00:01:18.344
We still have the one bullet left.

00:01:57.591 --> 00:01:58.914
Get back

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.352
Or I'll kill you. I swear to god.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:02.859
You won't.

00:02:02.863 --> 00:02:05.999
You're saving that
bullet for someone else.

00:02:09.029 --> 00:02:10.177
You want to bet?

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:34.141
Oh, my god!

00:02:34.144 --> 00:02:35.478
Dad...

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.038
Did I do this? Dad...

00:02:40.753 --> 00:02:42.281
Dean...

00:02:56.604 --> 00:02:58.816
Significant passenger, space intrusion.

00:02:58.821 --> 00:03:01.778
Unresponsive. B.P. 180 over 50.

00:03:01.793 --> 00:03:05.211
B.P. 100 over 15. Heartbeat 95.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.842
Tell me if they're okay!
You have to stay still.

00:03:07.846 --> 00:03:09.147
Are they even alive!

00:03:36.109 --> 00:03:37.350
Sam?

00:03:44.652 --> 00:03:45.781
Dad?

00:03:47.765 --> 00:03:49.002
Anybody?!

00:03:55.665 --> 00:03:59.002
Shadow county, nurses' station.
How can I transfer your call?

00:03:59.953 --> 00:04:01.645
Of course.

00:04:01.649 --> 00:04:03.128
I transfer your call.

00:04:06.608 --> 00:04:08.540
Excuse me.

00:04:14.841 --> 00:04:16.422
Hi.

00:04:16.565 --> 00:04:20.107
I, uh... I think I was in
a car accident with my...

00:04:20.473 --> 00:04:22.755
Dad and my brother. I
just need to find them.

00:04:28.372 --> 00:04:29.190
Hello?

00:05:21.953 --> 00:05:22.973
Sammy...

00:05:24.281 --> 00:05:25.462
You look good...

00:05:26.149 --> 00:05:27.288
Considering...

00:05:36.379 --> 00:05:38.111
Man, tell me you can hear me.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.038
How's dad?

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:45.528
Is he okay?

00:05:47.272 --> 00:05:48.793
Come on, you're the psychic.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.623
Give me some ghost
whispering or something.

00:05:52.592 --> 00:05:53.730
Your father's awake.

00:05:55.616 --> 00:05:57.023
You can go see him if you like.

00:05:57.591 --> 00:05:58.842
Oh, thank god.

00:06:01.278 --> 00:06:02.766
Doc, what about my brother?

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:04.975
Well, he sustained serious injury.

00:06:04.981 --> 00:06:07.395
Blood loss, contusions
to his liver and kidney.

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:09.312
But it's the head
trauma I'm worried about.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:11.540
There's early signs of cerebral edema.

00:06:11.546 --> 00:06:13.086
Well, what can we do?

00:06:13.102 --> 00:06:15.857
Well, we won't know his full
condition until he wakes up.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:18.339
If,

00:06:18.532 --> 00:06:19.886
He wakes up.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.289
If?

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:23.448
I have to be honest. Screw
you, doc I'm waking up!

00:06:23.453 --> 00:06:25.969
Most people with his degree of injury
wouldn't have survived this long.

00:06:26.183 --> 00:06:27.736
He's fighting very hard.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.897
But you need to have
realistic expectations, son.

00:06:31.514 --> 00:06:32.937
Come on, Sam.

00:06:32.941 --> 00:06:35.725
Go find some hoodoo priest
to lay some mojo on me.

00:06:35.732 --> 00:06:36.931
I'll be fine.

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:41.079
Sam?

00:06:43.289 --> 00:06:45.185
All right. Here.

00:06:45.899 --> 00:06:47.634
Give them my insurance.

00:06:49.453 --> 00:06:51.478
Elroy Mcgillicuddy?

00:06:52.255 --> 00:06:54.540
And his two loving sons.

00:06:56.905 --> 00:06:58.053
So...

00:06:59.533 --> 00:07:01.628
What else did the doctor say about Dean?

00:07:02.113 --> 00:07:03.485
N othing.

00:07:05.217 --> 00:07:06.184
Look...

00:07:06.441 --> 00:07:08.173
If the doctors won't do anything,

00:07:08.509 --> 00:07:10.190
Then we'll have to, that's all.

00:07:10.194 --> 00:07:11.929
I don't know. I'll find some...

00:07:12.707 --> 00:07:15.500
Hoodoo priest and lay some mojo on him.

00:07:17.083 --> 00:07:18.844
We'll  look for someone.

00:07:18.851 --> 00:07:20.192
Yeah.

00:07:20.357 --> 00:07:21.624
But, Sam...

00:07:22.854 --> 00:07:24.867
I don't know if we're gonna find anyone.

00:07:24.873 --> 00:07:25.951
Why not?

00:07:26.629 --> 00:07:28.374
I found that faith healer before.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.934
That was one in a million. So what?

00:07:30.936 --> 00:07:33.162
We just sit here with
our thumbs up our ass?

00:07:33.167 --> 00:07:34.546
No, I said we'd look.

00:07:36.136 --> 00:07:38.683
All right? I'll check under every stone.

00:07:43.317 --> 00:07:44.474
Where's the colt?

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.510
Your son is dying,

00:07:48.515 --> 00:07:50.900
And you're worried about
the colt? We are hunting

00:07:50.905 --> 00:07:53.501
This demon, and maybe
it's hunting us too.

00:07:54.109 --> 00:07:56.481
That  gun may be our only card.

00:07:57.834 --> 00:07:59.233
It's in the trunk.

00:08:00.363 --> 00:08:02.594
They dragged the car
to a yard off of i-83.

00:08:02.602 --> 00:08:06.028
All right, you got to clean out that trunk
before some junk man sees what's inside.

00:08:06.034 --> 00:08:07.374
I already called Bobby.

00:08:07.541 --> 00:08:10.940
He's like an hour out. He's gonna
tow the Impala back to his place.

00:08:10.942 --> 00:08:12.234
All right. You,

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:15.455
You go meet up with Bobby. You get
that colt and bring it back to me.

00:08:15.462 --> 00:08:17.706
And you watch out for hospital security.

00:08:17.721 --> 00:08:19.222
I think I got it covered.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.428
Hey.

00:08:28.693 --> 00:08:29.510
Here.

00:08:31.141 --> 00:08:32.464
I made a list of things I need

00:08:32.466 --> 00:08:34.371
That Bobby pick them up for me.

00:08:36.131 --> 00:08:37.079
Acacia?

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.485
Oil of Abramelin? What's this stuff for?

00:08:40.491 --> 00:08:41.477
Protection.

00:08:46.342 --> 00:08:47.452
Hey, dad...

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.460
You know the demon?

00:08:49.645 --> 00:08:52.911
He said he had plans for
me and children like me.

00:08:53.037 --> 00:08:55.011
You have any idea what he meant by that?

00:08:55.747 --> 00:08:57.611
No, I don't.

00:09:08.308 --> 00:09:10.792
Well, you sure know something.

00:09:14.281 --> 00:09:15.671
Oh, man.

00:09:16.017 --> 00:09:18.102
Dean is gonna be pissed.

00:09:23.699 --> 00:09:25.530
Look, Sam, this...

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.671
This just ain't worth a tow.

00:09:33.476 --> 00:09:36.654
I say we empty the trunk,
and sell the rest for scrap.

00:09:39.208 --> 00:09:40.057
No.

00:09:42.627 --> 00:09:44.077
Dean would kill me if we did that.

00:09:45.566 --> 00:09:47.504
When he gets better, he's
gonna want to fix this.

00:09:48.773 --> 00:09:50.568
There's nothing to fix.

00:09:51.328 --> 00:09:53.902
The frame's a pretzel.
The engine's ruined.

00:09:54.648 --> 00:09:56.884
There's barely any
parts worth salvaging.

00:09:57.289 --> 00:09:58.289
Listen to me, Bobby.

00:09:59.507 --> 00:10:01.580
If there's only one
working part, that's enough.

00:10:02.591 --> 00:10:04.351
We're not just gonna give up on...

00:10:08.535 --> 00:10:09.744
Okay.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:11.432
You got it.

00:10:13.683 --> 00:10:14.992
Here...

00:10:15.179 --> 00:10:17.374
Dad asked if you could
get this stuff for him.

00:10:19.918 --> 00:10:21.458
What John want with this?

00:10:21.956 --> 00:10:23.697
Protection from the demon.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.889
What?

00:10:29.404 --> 00:10:32.102
Nothing. It's just... Bobby.

00:10:34.283 --> 00:10:35.704
What's going on?

00:10:52.246 --> 00:10:53.466
Come on, dad.

00:10:54.502 --> 00:10:55.893
You got to help me.

00:10:57.918 --> 00:11:00.240
I got to get better. I
got to get back in there.

00:11:06.148 --> 00:11:08.202
I mean, you haven't
called a soul for help.

00:11:08.941 --> 00:11:10.503
You haven't even tried.

00:11:10.989 --> 00:11:12.389
Aren't you gonna do anything?

00:11:13.187 --> 00:11:14.870
Aren't you gonna even say anything?!

00:11:18.739 --> 00:11:20.930
I've done everything
you have ever asked me.

00:11:21.709 --> 00:11:22.881
Everything.

00:11:23.047 --> 00:11:25.268
I've given everything I've ever had.

00:11:27.242 --> 00:11:29.737
Now you're just gonna sit
there? You're gonna watch me die?

00:11:32.231 --> 00:11:34.255
I mean, what the hell
kind of father are you?!

00:11:42.222 --> 00:11:43.571
What is that?

00:11:50.183 --> 00:11:51.631
I take it you didn't see that.

00:12:23.231 --> 00:12:24.239
Hey!

00:12:24.484 --> 00:12:26.129
I need some help in here!

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:29.850
I can't...

00:12:30.087 --> 00:12:31.195
Breathe.

00:12:42.014 --> 00:12:44.267
Sammy, tell me you can
freaking hear me, man.

00:12:44.275 --> 00:12:45.464
There's something in the hospital.

00:12:45.468 --> 00:12:47.721
Now, you got to bring me back,
and we got to hunt this thing.

00:12:47.999 --> 00:12:49.067
Sam!

00:12:49.554 --> 00:12:50.694
You're quiet.

00:12:55.939 --> 00:12:57.589
You think I wouldn't find out?

00:12:57.597 --> 00:12:59.345
What are you talking about?
That stuff from Bobby.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:02.118
You don't use it to ward off a
demon. You use it to summon one.

00:13:02.415 --> 00:13:04.065
You're planning on bringing
the demon here, aren't you?

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:06.353
Having some stupid macho showdown!

00:13:06.368 --> 00:13:09.316
I have a plan, Sam.
That's exactly my point!

00:13:09.323 --> 00:13:11.977
Dean is dying, and you have a plan!

00:13:12.184 --> 00:13:13.764
You know what?! You care more about

00:13:13.769 --> 00:13:16.235
Killing this demon than
you do saving your own son!

00:13:16.239 --> 00:13:18.232
No, no, no. Guys, don't do
this! Do not tell me how I feel!

00:13:18.237 --> 00:13:20.691
I am doing this for Dean. How?

00:13:21.015 --> 00:13:22.807
How is revenge gonna help him?

00:13:22.813 --> 00:13:24.837
You're not thinking about
anybody but yourself!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.184
It's the same selfish obsession!

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:28.710
Come on, guys, don't
do this! That's funny,

00:13:28.748 --> 00:13:30.959
I thought this was your
obsession too. This demon

00:13:31.005 --> 00:13:32.437
Killed your mother,

00:13:32.442 --> 00:13:35.859
Killed your girlfriend. You
begged me to be part of this hunt!

00:13:35.865 --> 00:13:38.479
Now, if you killed that damn
thing when you had the chance,

00:13:38.486 --> 00:13:40.761
None of this would have happened.
It was possessing you, dad!

00:13:40.763 --> 00:13:41.923
I would have killed you, too! Yeah,

00:13:41.929 --> 00:13:43.722
And your brother would
be awake right now.

00:13:43.724 --> 00:13:45.458
Shut up, both of you! Go to hell.

00:13:45.674 --> 00:13:48.167
I should have never taken
you along in the first place.

00:13:48.173 --> 00:13:50.778
I knew it was a mistake.
I said "shut up!"

00:13:58.625 --> 00:14:00.545
Dude, I full-On swayzed that mother.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.701
What is it?

00:14:14.706 --> 00:14:16.176
Something's going on out there.

00:14:20.228 --> 00:14:22.121
All clear? Clear.

00:14:23.491 --> 00:14:25.201
Still no pulse. No.

00:14:25.648 --> 00:14:27.119
Still no pulse.

00:14:27.126 --> 00:14:29.730
Okay, let's go again. 360. Charging.

00:14:29.746 --> 00:14:32.011
All clear? Clear.

00:14:32.465 --> 00:14:35.243
Come on, come on... Still no pulse.

00:14:37.286 --> 00:14:38.264
Clear.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:43.584
Still nothing. Okay, let's go again.

00:14:44.704 --> 00:14:45.994
Charging.

00:14:45.999 --> 00:14:46.836
All clear?

00:14:46.843 --> 00:14:49.386
Get the hell away from me. Stay back!

00:14:51.844 --> 00:14:54.014
There's no change. Starting cpr.

00:14:54.022 --> 00:14:55.321
I said get back!

00:15:01.671 --> 00:15:03.042
Still nothing.

00:15:11.139 --> 00:15:12.027
We have a pulse.

00:15:12.353 --> 00:15:13.883
We're back into sinus rhythm.

00:15:31.769 --> 00:15:32.927
Don't worry, Sammy.

00:15:33.435 --> 00:15:34.864
I'm not going anywhere.

00:15:35.562 --> 00:15:37.296
I'm getting that thing
before it gets me.

00:15:40.452 --> 00:15:41.721
It's some kind of spirit,

00:15:42.481 --> 00:15:43.669
But I could grab it.

00:15:44.379 --> 00:15:45.477
And if I can grab it,

00:15:46.175 --> 00:15:47.134
I can kill it.

00:16:04.567 --> 00:16:06.039
Can't you see me?!

00:16:07.376 --> 00:16:09.262
Why won't you look at me?!

00:16:10.621 --> 00:16:11.800
Now what?

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:17.202
Somebody talk to me!

00:16:17.205 --> 00:16:20.353
Say something, please! Can you see me?

00:16:21.281 --> 00:16:22.219
Yeah.

00:16:25.349 --> 00:16:27.442
All right, just calm down.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.079
What's your name?

00:16:29.084 --> 00:16:30.133
Tessa.

00:16:30.297 --> 00:16:31.959
Okay, good, Tessa. I'm Dean.

00:16:32.476 --> 00:16:34.286
What's happening to me?

00:16:35.208 --> 00:16:36.187
Am I...

00:16:36.461 --> 00:16:37.800
Am I dead?

00:16:37.807 --> 00:16:39.326
That sort of depends.

00:16:50.277 --> 00:16:51.805
I don't understand.

00:16:52.184 --> 00:16:54.357
I just came in for an appendectomy.

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.514
I hate to bear bad news, but...

00:16:59.373 --> 00:17:01.274
I think there were some complications.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:06.133
It's just a dream, that's all.

00:17:06.138 --> 00:17:07.647
This is just

00:17:07.653 --> 00:17:09.366
A very weird,

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.612
Unbelievably vivid dream.

00:17:11.618 --> 00:17:12.717
Tessa,

00:17:13.167 --> 00:17:14.476
It's not a dream.

00:17:14.732 --> 00:17:16.292
Then what else could it be?

00:17:18.587 --> 00:17:20.701
You ever heard of an
out-Of-Body experience?

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.832
What are you, some new-Agey guy?

00:17:23.835 --> 00:17:26.573
You see me messing with
crystals or listening to Yanni?

00:17:28.454 --> 00:17:30.289
It's actually a very old idea.

00:17:30.864 --> 00:17:32.535
It's got a lot of different names.

00:17:32.753 --> 00:17:34.012
Bilocation,

00:17:34.518 --> 00:17:36.683
Crisis apparitions, fetches.

00:17:36.887 --> 00:17:38.598
I think it's happening to us.

00:17:38.915 --> 00:17:40.216
If it is...

00:17:41.678 --> 00:17:43.417
It  means that we're spirits...

00:17:44.188 --> 00:17:46.109
Of people close to death.

00:17:48.805 --> 00:17:50.347
So we're gonna die?

00:17:50.481 --> 00:17:51.380
No.

00:17:52.119 --> 00:17:53.197
Not if we hold on.

00:17:53.634 --> 00:17:56.468
Our bodies can get better. You can
snap right back in there and wake up.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.012
What do you mean you felt something?

00:18:02.015 --> 00:18:03.658
I mean, it felt like...

00:18:04.414 --> 00:18:05.543
Like Dean.

00:18:06.274 --> 00:18:08.588
Like he was there, just
out of eyeshot or something.

00:18:09.186 --> 00:18:11.137
I don't know if it's my
psychic thing or what.

00:18:11.411 --> 00:18:12.882
But do you think it's even possible?

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:15.352
Do you think his spirit could be around?

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.622
Anything's possible.

00:18:17.939 --> 00:18:19.621
Well, there's one way to find out.

00:18:20.299 --> 00:18:22.913
Where are you going? I got to

00:18:22.916 --> 00:18:25.722
Pick something up.
I'll be back. Wait, Sam.

00:18:25.728 --> 00:18:27.130
I promise

00:18:27.276 --> 00:18:29.006
I won't hunt this demon.

00:18:29.574 --> 00:18:31.629
Not until we know Dean's okay.

00:18:36.993 --> 00:18:38.606
I got to say, I'm impressed.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.402
With what? You.

00:18:40.777 --> 00:18:43.173
Most people in your spot
would be jello by now, but

00:18:43.176 --> 00:18:44.921
You're taking this pretty well.

00:18:44.926 --> 00:18:46.554
Maybe a little better than me.

00:18:46.832 --> 00:18:48.031
Don't get me wrong,

00:18:48.366 --> 00:18:50.500
I was pretty freaked at first. But

00:18:50.898 --> 00:18:53.072
Now I don't know. Maybe I'm dealing.

00:18:53.077 --> 00:18:54.626
So you're okay with dying?

00:18:54.633 --> 00:18:56.777
No, of course not.

00:18:57.574 --> 00:19:00.741
I  just think whatever's
gonna happen is gonna happen.

00:19:00.975 --> 00:19:03.160
It's out of my control. It's just...

00:19:03.164 --> 00:19:04.445
Fate.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:08.492
That's crap.

00:19:10.182 --> 00:19:11.853
You always have a choice.

00:19:12.383 --> 00:19:15.276
You can either roll over and die, you
can keep fighting no matter what...

00:19:15.293 --> 00:19:17.458
<i>Room 237. Code blue. Dr. Christie</i>

00:19:17.462 --> 00:19:19.486
Dean, where are you
going? Just wait here.

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:29.224
Give me another amp oepi, please.

00:19:37.931 --> 00:19:39.461
Get away from her!

00:19:39.961 --> 00:19:40.927
Still nothing.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.671
All right. Let's call it.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:51.558
Time of death...

00:19:51.726 --> 00:19:53.477
5:11 p.M.

00:19:54.998 --> 00:19:56.940
At least she's not suffering anymore.

00:20:12.525 --> 00:20:13.346
Hey.

00:20:15.057 --> 00:20:17.741
I think maybe you're
around. And if you are,

00:20:18.984 --> 00:20:20.502
Don't make fun of me for this,

00:20:20.509 --> 00:20:21.558
But, um...

00:20:23.439 --> 00:20:24.808
But there's one way we can talk.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:32.328
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:20:48.459 --> 00:20:49.395
Dean?

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.383
Dean, are you here?

00:21:01.219 --> 00:21:03.792
God, I feel like I'm at a slumber party.

00:21:06.368 --> 00:21:07.917
All right, Sam.

00:21:09.308 --> 00:21:11.081
This isn't gonna work.

00:21:29.048 --> 00:21:30.347
I'll be damned.

00:21:31.909 --> 00:21:33.911
Oh, it's good to hear from you, man.

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:36.964
It hasn't been the
same without you, Dean.

00:21:36.967 --> 00:21:38.276
Damn straight.

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:41.591
All right.

00:21:45.139 --> 00:21:46.116
Dean, what?

00:21:48.723 --> 00:21:49.663
" H"...

00:21:51.243 --> 00:21:52.012
"U"...

00:21:58.592 --> 00:21:59.780
"Hunt"?

00:22:00.077 --> 00:22:01.518
What, "hunting"?

00:22:01.523 --> 00:22:03.026
Are you hunting?

00:22:06.665 --> 00:22:10.060
Dean, it's in the hospital,
what you're hunting?

00:22:10.066 --> 00:22:11.869
Do you know what it is?

00:22:13.107 --> 00:22:15.021
One question at a time, dude.

00:22:16.091 --> 00:22:17.360
What is it?

00:22:21.771 --> 00:22:23.815
I don't think it's killing people.

00:22:24.361 --> 00:22:25.825
I think it's taking them...

00:22:27.072 --> 00:22:28.384
You know, when...

00:22:29.484 --> 00:22:30.953
When their time is just up.

00:22:33.699 --> 00:22:35.099
A reaper...

00:22:37.733 --> 00:22:39.227
Is it after you?

00:22:49.741 --> 00:22:51.303
If it's here naturally,

00:22:52.744 --> 00:22:54.334
There's no way to stop it.

00:22:55.313 --> 00:22:56.823
Yeah, you can't kill death.

00:22:57.604 --> 00:22:59.383
Man, you're, uh...

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:00.518
I'm screwed, Sam.

00:23:05.111 --> 00:23:06.822
No. No, no, no.

00:23:07.773 --> 00:23:09.242
There's got to be a way.

00:23:09.710 --> 00:23:11.109
There's got to be a way.

00:23:11.877 --> 00:23:13.398
Dad will know what to do.

00:23:23.241 --> 00:23:24.063
Dad?

00:24:17.074 --> 00:24:19.486
Hey, so dad wasn't in his room.

00:24:19.634 --> 00:24:20.823
Where is he?

00:24:20.829 --> 00:24:23.573
But I got dad's journal, so...

00:24:23.859 --> 00:24:26.005
Who knows? Maybe there's
something in here.

00:24:35.384 --> 00:24:37.430
Thanks for not giving up on me, Sammy.

00:24:55.664 --> 00:24:57.497
Son of a bitch.

00:25:05.423 --> 00:25:06.933
Hi, Dean.

00:25:07.702 --> 00:25:10.268
You know, you read the
most interesting things.

00:25:11.093 --> 00:25:13.571
For example, did you know that reapers

00:25:13.575 --> 00:25:15.566
Can alter human perception?

00:25:17.488 --> 00:25:18.660
I sure didn't.

00:25:20.661 --> 00:25:23.771
Basically they can make themselves
appear however they want...

00:25:24.850 --> 00:25:26.078
Like, say...

00:25:26.647 --> 00:25:28.028
A pretty girl.

00:25:29.860 --> 00:25:32.124
You're much prettier than
the last reaper I met.

00:25:32.229 --> 00:25:34.502
I was wondering when
you'd figure it out.

00:25:35.852 --> 00:25:37.314
I should have known.

00:25:38.413 --> 00:25:43.186
That whole "accepting fate" rap of yours
is far too laid-Back for a dead chick.

00:25:43.191 --> 00:25:46.719
But, you know, the mother and the body...
I'm still trying to figure that one out.

00:25:47.105 --> 00:25:49.059
It's my sandbox.

00:25:49.315 --> 00:25:51.125
I can make you see whatever I want.

00:25:51.133 --> 00:25:53.213
What is this, like a
turn-On for you, huh?

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:56.245
Toying with me? You
didn't give me much choice.

00:25:56.253 --> 00:25:58.708
You saw my true form,
and you flipped out.

00:25:59.697 --> 00:26:01.648
Kind of hurts a girl's feelings.

00:26:03.441 --> 00:26:06.475
This was the only way I
could get you to talk to me.

00:26:06.634 --> 00:26:07.660
Okay, fine.

00:26:08.348 --> 00:26:09.289
We're talking.

00:26:10.054 --> 00:26:11.757
What the hell do you want to talk about?

00:26:13.549 --> 00:26:15.410
How death is nothing to fear.

00:26:16.661 --> 00:26:18.384
It's your time to go, Dean.

00:26:20.096 --> 00:26:22.558
And you're living on
borrowed time already.

00:27:21.264 --> 00:27:22.917
What the hell are you
doing down here, buddy?

00:27:22.919 --> 00:27:24.383
I can explain. Yeah?

00:27:24.386 --> 00:27:27.725
You're gonna explain to
security. Come on. You follow me.

00:27:28.864 --> 00:27:29.884
Hey.

00:27:31.744 --> 00:27:33.436
How stupid you think I am?

00:27:36.405 --> 00:27:39.099
You really want an
honest answer to that?

00:27:50.359 --> 00:27:53.828
You conjuring me, John? I'm surprised.

00:27:53.832 --> 00:27:55.944
I took you for a lot of things,

00:27:55.950 --> 00:28:00.022
But suicidally reckless
wasn't one of them.

00:28:00.770 --> 00:28:02.502
I can always shoot you.

00:28:02.979 --> 00:28:04.710
You could always miss.

00:28:06.011 --> 00:28:08.643
And you only got one try, don't you?

00:28:11.593 --> 00:28:12.632
Did you

00:28:13.279 --> 00:28:15.149
Really think you could trap me?

00:28:16.358 --> 00:28:17.882
Oh, I don't want to trap you.

00:28:22.744 --> 00:28:24.134
I want to make a deal.

00:28:31.236 --> 00:28:32.349
Dean, are you here?

00:28:37.069 --> 00:28:38.842
Couldn't find anything in the book.

00:28:41.559 --> 00:28:43.178
I don't know how to help you.

00:28:46.439 --> 00:28:48.288
But I'll keep trying, all right?

00:28:49.049 --> 00:28:50.851
As long as you keep fighting.

00:28:54.450 --> 00:28:55.901
I mean, come on, you can't...

00:28:56.626 --> 00:28:59.935
You can't leave me here alone with dad.
We'll kill each other. You know that.

00:29:08.646 --> 00:29:10.445
Dean, you got to hold on.

00:29:13.103 --> 00:29:15.225
You can't go, man, not now.

00:29:17.849 --> 00:29:19.993
We were just starting
to be brothers again.

00:29:24.065 --> 00:29:25.494
Can you hear me?

00:29:27.690 --> 00:29:29.610
Look, I'm sure you've
heard this before, but...

00:29:31.111 --> 00:29:34.058
You got to make an exception.
You got to cut me a break.

00:29:34.795 --> 00:29:36.367
Stage 3...

00:29:36.372 --> 00:29:37.591
Bargaining.

00:29:40.308 --> 00:29:41.770
I'm serious.

00:29:43.412 --> 00:29:45.343
My family is in danger.

00:29:46.323 --> 00:29:48.254
See, we're kind of in
the middle of this, uh...

00:29:48.833 --> 00:29:50.512
War.

00:29:50.879 --> 00:29:53.634
And they need me. The fight's over.

00:29:53.639 --> 00:29:56.314
No, it isn't. It is for you.

00:29:57.002 --> 00:29:58.616
Dean...

00:29:58.760 --> 00:30:01.777
You're not the first soldier
I've plucked from the field.

00:30:02.463 --> 00:30:03.896
They all feel the same.

00:30:04.534 --> 00:30:06.354
They can't leave.

00:30:06.561 --> 00:30:09.107
Victory hangs in the balance.

00:30:09.152 --> 00:30:10.440
But they're wrong.

00:30:11.391 --> 00:30:14.227
The battle goes on
without them. My brother,

00:30:14.231 --> 00:30:15.641
He could die without me.

00:30:15.906 --> 00:30:17.390
Maybe he will.

00:30:18.127 --> 00:30:19.649
Maybe he won't.

00:30:20.516 --> 00:30:22.718
Nothing you can do about it.

00:30:28.467 --> 00:30:30.431
It's an honorable death,

00:30:30.995 --> 00:30:32.769
A warrior's death.

00:30:33.818 --> 00:30:36.403
I think I'll pass on
the 72 virgins, thanks.

00:30:37.179 --> 00:30:39.324
I'm not that into prude chicks anyway.

00:30:39.329 --> 00:30:40.901
That's funny.

00:30:41.016 --> 00:30:42.445
You're very cute.

00:30:44.377 --> 00:30:46.643
There's no such thing
as an honorable death.

00:30:47.652 --> 00:30:51.091
My corpse is gonna rot in the
ground, and my family is gonna die.

00:30:54.105 --> 00:30:55.396
No.

00:30:58.054 --> 00:31:00.427
I'm not going with you.
I don't care what you do.

00:31:03.393 --> 00:31:04.340
Well,

00:31:04.688 --> 00:31:06.188
Like you said...

00:31:07.247 --> 00:31:08.909
There's always a choice.

00:31:09.345 --> 00:31:11.508
I can't make you come with me.

00:31:12.039 --> 00:31:13.248
But,

00:31:13.916 --> 00:31:15.979
You're not getting back in your body.

00:31:16.727 --> 00:31:18.347
And that's just facts.

00:31:19.325 --> 00:31:20.614
So, yes,

00:31:20.622 --> 00:31:21.899
You can stay.

00:31:22.016 --> 00:31:23.958
You'll stay here for years...

00:31:24.505 --> 00:31:25.847
Disembodied.

00:31:26.000 --> 00:31:27.283
Scared.

00:31:27.396 --> 00:31:30.285
And over the decades, it'll
probably drive you mad.

00:31:31.172 --> 00:31:33.346
Maybe you'll even get violent.

00:31:33.503 --> 00:31:35.184
What are you saying?

00:31:38.268 --> 00:31:40.695
How do you think angry spirits are born?

00:31:42.094 --> 00:31:43.637
They can't let go,

00:31:43.651 --> 00:31:45.404
And they can't move on.

00:31:45.689 --> 00:31:47.743
And you're about to become one.

00:31:48.611 --> 00:31:50.633
The same thing you hunt.

00:31:54.213 --> 00:31:56.365
It's very unsinly,

00:31:56.370 --> 00:31:58.123
Making deals with devils.

00:32:00.066 --> 00:32:02.872
How do I know this
isn't just another trick?

00:32:02.985 --> 00:32:04.607
It's no trick.

00:32:05.787 --> 00:32:07.558
I will give you the colt

00:32:07.955 --> 00:32:09.366
And the bullet.

00:32:10.045 --> 00:32:12.106
But you got to help Dean.

00:32:13.971 --> 00:32:15.883
You got to bring him back.

00:32:16.752 --> 00:32:19.528
Why, John, you're a sentimentalist.

00:32:21.400 --> 00:32:22.810
If only your boys

00:32:23.254 --> 00:32:25.157
Knew how much their daddy loved them.

00:32:25.864 --> 00:32:27.308
It's a good trade.

00:32:28.647 --> 00:32:32.187
You care hell of a lot more
about this gun than you do Dean.

00:32:32.189 --> 00:32:33.441
Don't be so sure.

00:32:34.056 --> 00:32:36.624
He killed some people
very special to me.

00:32:38.816 --> 00:32:41.159
But, still, you're right.
He isn't much of a threat.

00:32:41.167 --> 00:32:44.223
And neither is your other son,

00:32:44.338 --> 00:32:45.446
Of course.

00:32:49.177 --> 00:32:50.657
You know the truth,

00:32:50.661 --> 00:32:51.714
Right?

00:32:53.233 --> 00:32:54.735
About Sammy...

00:32:55.333 --> 00:32:56.770
And the other children?

00:32:57.238 --> 00:32:58.116
Yeah.

00:32:58.634 --> 00:33:00.324
I've known for a while.

00:33:00.332 --> 00:33:04.112
But Sam doesn't, does he?
You've been playing dumb.

00:33:04.666 --> 00:33:06.622
Can you bring Dean back?

00:33:07.216 --> 00:33:09.292
Yes or no.

00:33:09.295 --> 00:33:10.504
No.

00:33:11.526 --> 00:33:13.325
But I know someone who can.

00:33:14.447 --> 00:33:15.785
It's not a problem.

00:33:16.666 --> 00:33:17.555
Good.

00:33:18.272 --> 00:33:20.282
And before I give you the gun,

00:33:20.862 --> 00:33:23.257
I'm gonna want to make
sure that Dean's okay,

00:33:23.271 --> 00:33:24.903
With my own eyes.

00:33:24.905 --> 00:33:26.801
Oh, John, I'm offended.

00:33:26.804 --> 00:33:28.334
Don't you trust me?

00:33:33.150 --> 00:33:34.097
Fine.

00:33:35.678 --> 00:33:39.116
So we have a deal? No, John, not yet.

00:33:39.123 --> 00:33:41.719
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:33:42.154 --> 00:33:43.485
With what?

00:33:45.507 --> 00:33:48.736
There's something else I want

00:33:49.061 --> 00:33:50.534
As much as that gun.

00:33:52.021 --> 00:33:53.352
Maybe more.

00:33:55.647 --> 00:33:57.600
It's time to put the pain behind you.

00:34:00.806 --> 00:34:02.136
And go where?

00:34:03.537 --> 00:34:04.597
Sorry.

00:34:05.477 --> 00:34:07.828
I can't give away the big punch line.

00:34:13.887 --> 00:34:15.219
Moment of truth.

00:34:17.160 --> 00:34:18.945
No changing your mind later.

00:34:22.081 --> 00:34:23.734
So, what's it going to be?

00:34:44.821 --> 00:34:46.241
What are you doing that for?

00:34:47.259 --> 00:34:48.369
I'm not doing it.

00:34:50.181 --> 00:34:51.641
What the hell...!

00:34:51.648 --> 00:34:53.177
You can't do this!

00:34:53.354 --> 00:34:54.824
Get away!

00:34:55.212 --> 00:34:56.810
What's happening?!

00:35:07.197 --> 00:35:09.118
Today's your lucky day, kid.

00:35:12.929 --> 00:35:13.969
Dean!

00:35:15.056 --> 00:35:16.942
Help! I need help!

00:35:18.724 --> 00:35:19.850
I can't explain it.

00:35:20.036 --> 00:35:21.356
The edema has vanished.

00:35:21.524 --> 00:35:23.516
The internal contusions are healed.

00:35:23.903 --> 00:35:25.171
Your vitals are good.

00:35:26.260 --> 00:35:28.425
You got to have some kind
of angel watching over you.

00:35:29.012 --> 00:35:30.202
Thanks, doc.

00:35:34.623 --> 00:35:36.204
You said a reaper was after me?

00:35:36.210 --> 00:35:37.079
Yeah.

00:35:37.425 --> 00:35:38.523
How did I ditch it?

00:35:38.700 --> 00:35:39.798
You got me.

00:35:41.101 --> 00:35:42.723
Dean, you really don't
remember anything?

00:35:43.169 --> 00:35:44.056
No.

00:35:44.806 --> 00:35:45.915
Except this

00:35:46.230 --> 00:35:47.711
Pit in my stomach.

00:35:49.020 --> 00:35:50.610
Sam, something's wrong.

00:35:54.150 --> 00:35:55.610
How you feeling, dude?

00:35:56.249 --> 00:35:57.478
Fine, I guess.

00:35:58.416 --> 00:35:59.498
I'm alive.

00:35:59.623 --> 00:36:01.364
That's what matters.

00:36:01.769 --> 00:36:03.071
Where were you last night?

00:36:05.847 --> 00:36:07.559
I had some things to take care of.

00:36:08.027 --> 00:36:09.535
Well, that's specific.

00:36:10.223 --> 00:36:11.704
Come on, Sam.

00:36:12.474 --> 00:36:14.112
Did you go after the demon?

00:36:16.077 --> 00:36:17.034
No.

00:36:17.041 --> 00:36:19.646
You know, why don't I
believe you right now?

00:36:26.147 --> 00:36:27.797
Can we not fight?

00:36:29.450 --> 00:36:32.698
You know, half the time we're fighting,
I don't know what we're fighting about.

00:36:32.703 --> 00:36:34.021
We're just butting heads.

00:36:35.513 --> 00:36:37.487
Look, Sammy, I've...

00:36:37.924 --> 00:36:39.764
I've made some mistakes.

00:36:41.297 --> 00:36:44.021
But I've always done the best I could.

00:36:45.843 --> 00:36:47.907
I just don't want to
fight anymore, okay?

00:36:49.857 --> 00:36:51.590
Dad, are you all right?

00:36:54.495 --> 00:36:55.655
Yeah.

00:36:56.145 --> 00:36:57.937
Yeah, I'm just a little tired.

00:36:59.435 --> 00:37:01.258
Hey, son, would you mind, uh...

00:37:02.177 --> 00:37:04.492
Would you mind getting
me a cup of caffeine?

00:37:04.545 --> 00:37:06.720
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:37:28.301 --> 00:37:29.771
What is it?

00:37:31.801 --> 00:37:33.114
You know, when, uh...

00:37:33.892 --> 00:37:35.513
When you were a kid,

00:37:37.597 --> 00:37:39.368
I'd come home from a hunt,

00:37:40.766 --> 00:37:43.624
And after what I'd seen, I'd be...

00:37:44.682 --> 00:37:46.264
I'd be wrecked.

00:37:47.114 --> 00:37:48.776
And you...

00:37:49.805 --> 00:37:51.634
You'd come up to me, and

00:37:51.639 --> 00:37:54.806
You'd put your hand on my shoulder, and
you'd look me in the eye, and you'd...

00:38:00.174 --> 00:38:02.146
You'd say, "it's okay, dad".

00:38:10.052 --> 00:38:11.884
I'm sorry.

00:38:13.556 --> 00:38:15.368
Why?

00:38:17.712 --> 00:38:21.524
You shouldn't have had to say that to
me. I should've been saying that to you.

00:38:23.244 --> 00:38:24.906
You know, I put...

00:38:26.144 --> 00:38:30.005
I put too much on your shoulders.
I made you grow up too fast.

00:38:31.707 --> 00:38:34.361
You took care of Sammy.
You took care of me.

00:38:36.015 --> 00:38:37.826
You did that.

00:38:38.542 --> 00:38:40.527
And you didn't complain. Not once.

00:38:45.540 --> 00:38:47.877
I just want you to know...

00:38:49.054 --> 00:38:51.509
That I am so proud of you.

00:38:54.689 --> 00:38:56.619
Is it really you talking?

00:38:56.623 --> 00:38:57.533
Yeah.

00:38:57.948 --> 00:38:59.630
Yeah, it's really me.

00:39:01.544 --> 00:39:03.566
Why are you saying this stuff?

00:39:11.873 --> 00:39:14.770
I want you to watch out for Sammy, okay?

00:39:15.711 --> 00:39:17.562
Yeah, dad, you know I will.

00:39:18.733 --> 00:39:20.130
You're scaring me.

00:39:21.925 --> 00:39:23.905
Don't be scared, Dean.

00:40:21.627 --> 00:40:22.697
Okay.

00:40:35.852 --> 00:40:36.852
Dad?

00:40:57.629 --> 00:40:59.722
No, no, no, it's our dad. It's our dad!

00:41:01.913 --> 00:41:04.178
Okay. Let's try again.
An amp of atropine.

00:41:04.182 --> 00:41:05.062
Come on...

00:41:11.561 --> 00:41:13.163
Okay. Stop compression.

00:41:20.728 --> 00:41:22.743
Come on, come on. Still no pulse.

00:41:24.103 --> 00:41:26.517
Okay. That's it,
everybody. I'll call it.

00:41:27.967 --> 00:41:30.674
Time of death, 10:41 a.M.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.769
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
